//OUT="hi 5"

// The right-hand side of a destructuring assignment is lowered once. It used to
// be lowered again together with the assignments built from it, and a string
// literal does not survive that: it came out as
// `_Str_from_raw(_Str_from_raw(<string>))`, which has no candidate, and the
// program was rejected. A variable is unchanged by a second lowering, which is
// why this has to be a literal.
//
// 08_structs/42 is the same thing through a struct pattern.

fn main
    a, b = "hi", 5
    out "{a} {b}"
